4. Setup & Local DevelopmentPrerequisitesBun installed locally (v1.0 or higher recommended).Installation & ExecutionBash# 1. Install project dependencies
bun install

# 2. Start the local development server with hot module reloading
bun dev

# 3. Build for production
bun run build
5. Design System & TokensAll core theme parameters are defined via CSS variables in src/styles.css using the modern oklch color space:Color TokensBase Canvas (--background): oklch(0.135 0.014 240) — Near-black slate providing high contrast for glowing overlays.Primary Accent (--primary): oklch(0.84 0.145 205) — Electric cyan for active states, track tags, and borders.Secondary Accent (--secondary): oklch(0.625 0.255 17) — Signal red-orange for countdown timers, "LIVE" tags, and critical CTAs.TypographyHeadings (font-display): Archivo, sans-serif (heavy weights: 700, 800, 900)Body & Telemetry (font-body): Space Grotesk, monospace/sans-serif (regular & medium weights)Key Animations (src/styles.css)Signal Sweep: A sweeping gradient simulation across card borders.Scan Line: Vertical linear sweep simulating CRT monitor refresh displays.Ticker: Seamless infinite marquee for quick updates or sponsor ribbons.Tech Grid: Background SVG/CSS radial mask for subtle perspective grids.6. Content Configuration & Release ManagementThe application is structured so non-engineering coordinators can update festival reveals directly inside src/routes/index.tsx.Track Releases (trackReveals)Controls the high-level streams (e.g., Computer Science, Robotics, Design):TypeScript// src/routes/index.tsx
export const trackReveals = [
